 "description": "A third continuation scored by each statistic's chance of failing (description; discarded seeds).\n\nThe second continuation (`hinge2.py`) passed its verdict at the threshold (the wild type in 3 of 5\npopulations, every mutant in 5 of 5), but its answer passes the wild type in only 6 of 10 fresh\npopulations (`robustness_check.json`). Three of the four failures are the on-lawn onset rate,\nwhose mean (z -3.08, SD 0.15) drifted onto its bar: the quadratic hinge, 5 x excess^2, costs only\n0.14 for 0.17 past a target, so the search traded the onset rate for gains elsewhere.\n\nFrom that answer, with its search state carried over (sigma and per-parameter steps at its end),\nsep-CMA on the same objective (stage 3's six families plus tph-1's, pdfr-1's and tax-4's lawn\ndifferences, the mutants half of it, both guards) plus each statistic's estimated chance of\nfailing a population: 10 x the sum over statistics of Phi((|z| - bar) / SD), z the statistic's own\nas the grade reads it, bar its pass rule's (3.0781 for a wild-type statistic, 2.24 for a mutant's),\nSD its spread between populations (the larger of `noise_measure.json`'s, 15 populations at the\nfirst continuation's answer, and `robustness_check.json`'s, 10 at the second's; floored at 0.05).\nThe sum is about the expected number of failing statistics, so the penalty is steep for a statistic\nwith little noise near its bar and soft for a noisy one. The plan was a steeper hinge, 5 x (excess +\nexcess^2) past targets 0.5 or more inside the bars; on the measured noise its per-candidate spread\nfrom pre-exit enrichment alone (SD 12) was four times the onset rate's whole signal (3 points),\nwhere this penalty's signal (4.6 points) stands near its noise from every statistic (about 4).\n50 generations, population 48 at 200 animals on 16 workers, readouts every 10\ngenerations with every statistic recorded. The verdict as stage 3's: the last answer graded with\npresence on 5 fresh populations passes the wild type in at least 3 and tph-1 and tax-4 each in at\nleast 3; then `robustness_check.py` grades it on 10 more.\n\nSeeds: candidates 868,000,000 + 200\u00b7k + i, CMA 9502, readouts 869,000,000 + i, the verdict\n870,000,000 + 200\u00b7g + i, the 10-population check 871,000,000 + 200\u00b7g + i. Run from the repository\nroot.\n",
